    add('mastercard-supernodes','Mastercard','Sum binary-tree supernodes defined by child digit sums',
        'A binary tree is represented by its root value and path-labelled nodes: L/R means left/right from the root, and longer paths such as LL or RRL continue those steps. A node is a supernode if it has both children and the sum of decimal digits of its left child equals that of its right child. Return the sum of the values of all supernodes.',None,
        'Store each node value under its root-relative path, with the root at the empty path. For every path p with both p+L and p+R present, compare their digit sums and add the parent value when equal. Leaves and one-child nodes cannot qualify. O(total path characters+N×D) time and O(total path characters) space, where D is the largest digit count.',
        section='dsa',topic='trees',type='coding',sources=['IMG-20240812-WA0016.jpg','IMG-20240812-WA0017.jpg','IMG-20240812-WA0020.jpg'],constraints='3 ≤ N ≤ 100.',input_format='N, root value, then N−1 lines containing path and node value.',output_format='The sum of supernode values.',
        examples=[{'input':'8\n21\nL 14\nR 23\nLL 7\nLR 70\nRR 11\nRRL 23\nRRR 32','output':'46'},{'input':'6\n11\nL 14\nR 23\nLL 7\nLR 8\nRR 14','output':'11'}],notes='The source does not specify signed node-value bounds; the shown examples use positive values.')
